From: SamuriHL <samurihl@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 08:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vh265: at end of stream, flush the other layer of a dual-layer pair

A dual-layer (Dolby Vision FEL/MEL) stream-mode pair runs one layer at a
time and hands over only when one parser finds the other layer's next
unit (switch_dvlayer_flag). When the player ends the stream
(AMSTREAM_SET_EOS) the layer running at that moment takes DEC_RESULT_EOS
and flushes its own reorder buffer, keeps sched, and its run_ready
returns 0 from then on: the other layer never runs again and its last
pictures stay in its reorder buffer, while the Dolby Vision path holds
the base pictures waiting for their pairs. The last pictures of a FEL
file or disc segment never show (FEL_test_for_AVS.m2ts: two). Either
layer can be the one that ends: the base on one run, the enhancement
layer on the next.

Flush the partner from the EOS branch, exactly as the ISR's "no el
anymore" path already flushes the enhancement layer, and say so.

---
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h265/vh265.c
@@ -14738,6 +14738,32 @@
 		hevc_print(hevc, PRINT_FLAG_VDEC_STATUS,
 			"%s: end of stream, last dec poc %d => 0x%pf\n",
 			__func__, hevc->curr_POC, pic);
+		/* Dual-layer: the two layers run only when one's parser hands over
+		 * to the other, which never happens again once this one has ended
+		 * - whichever it is (the stream ends in the enhancement layer when
+		 * its last unit is the EL's). Flush the partner here, as the "no el
+		 * anymore" path in the ISR does for the enhancement layer, so its
+		 * last pictures come out and every base picture finds its pair. */
+		if ((vdec->slave && vdec->slave->private) ||
+			(vdec->master && vdec->master->private)) {
+			struct vdec_s *partner =
+				vdec->slave ? vdec->slave : vdec->master;
+			struct hevc_state_s *hevc_p =
+				(struct hevc_state_s *)partner->private;
+			struct PIC_s *p_pic;
+
+			check_pic_decoded_error(hevc_p,
+				hevc_p->pic_decoded_lcu_idx);
+			p_pic = get_pic_by_POC(hevc_p, hevc_p->curr_POC);
+			hevc_p->curr_POC = INVALID_POC;
+			hevc_p->m_pocRandomAccess = MAX_INT;
+			flush_output(hevc_p, p_pic);
+			hevc_p->decoded_poc = INVALID_POC;
+			hevc_p->decoding_pic = NULL;
+			pr_info("vh265: end of stream in the %s layer: flushed the %s layer\n",
+				vdec->slave ? "base" : "enhancement",
+				vdec->slave ? "enhancement" : "base");
+		}
 		flush_output(hevc, pic);
 		/* dummy vf with eos flag to backend */
 		notify_v4l_eos(hw_to_vdec(hevc));
